                <pb facs="0418" n="410" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg410"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/14275: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-08-23T00:00:00+01:00">August 23,
                        1941—midnight</date>.<lb/>[Received August 23—8:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3840. Personal for the Secretary of State. This morning I talked with Mr. Eden.
                    He wanted you to know how seriously they view the <pb facs="0419" n="411"
                        xml:id="pg411"/> German agents in Iran. The British are certain that their
                    negotiations with the Iran Government are being directed by the Germans. I felt
                    Mr. Eden was simply asking for a sympathetic understanding of their problem.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
